      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & 3 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
