      ":question/id": "9752715d-a11c-5d27-95dc-d20bec1117cb",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73439",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=2 \\\\ y &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3(1)=2\\,⇒\\,x=2-3=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=1.$"
    }
